        <h3 class="cag-h3">Jins, Male, and Jeni, Female — Unrelated and Raised Alongside Each Other</h3>
        <p>Jins is a male of about six months and Jeni a female of about four. They come from different parents, they were hand-fed by us, and they have shared space since weaning. They are not a mated pair and they are years away from being one.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">What We Tell Every Buyer Who Asks About This Pair</h3>
        <p>We tell them what section six of this page says: these two meet every condition that produces a self-sufficient pair. If you take both, the protocol is not optional. If that sounds like more than you want to take on, take one.</p>

        <h4 class="cag-h4">Can You Buy Just One of Them?</h4>
        <p>Yes. Jins is $1,900 and Jeni is $1,800 on their own. We would rather place one bird into a household that will work with it than push two into a home that wanted one.</p>
        <h5 class="cag-h5">They Are Offered as a Pair, but Neither Is Held Hostage to the Other</h5>
        <p>The pair price exists because they are easy to place together, not because we refuse to separate them. Say which bird suits you and we will talk it through honestly.</p>
