      <!-- ═══ §14 BUILD YOUR OWN ═══ -->
      <section id="build-your-own">
        <h2 class="cag-h2">Which of Our Single Greys Pair Well Together?</h2>
        <p>If you want two birds but want both of them people-focused, this is the route we would steer you toward. Two singles, introduced under your own roof, on your own timetable.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">Roys and Amie, Both Congo, Both Available</h3>
        <p>Roys is a confident male at $2,300 and Amie a steadier female at $2,500. They are siblings out of James and Lois, which means they already know each other but were not raised as a bonded unit — a middle ground between a ready-made pair and two strangers.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">Elad and Evie, the Timneh Alternative</h3>
        <p><a href="/timneh-african-grey-for-sale/">Our Timneh pair option</a> is Elad at $1,600 and Evie at $1,500, both out of Levi and Rily. A Timneh is smaller, generally calmer and often talking earlier than a Congo, and two of them is the least expensive two-bird route we offer. ↗</p>

        <figure class="sec-img-wrap">
          <img class="sec-img og-photo" src={`${IMG}/congo-and-timneh-together-our-aviary.webp`} width="1408" height="768"
               alt="A Congo African Grey and a Timneh African Grey sharing a perch together in our own Midland aviary"
