      <div class="seam-wrap" aria-hidden="true"><img class="seam" src={seam} alt="" width="182" height="60" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
      <!-- ═══ §15 PAPERWORK ═══ -->
      <section id="papers">
        <h2 class="cag-h2">What Paperwork Travels With Each Bird in a Pair?</h2>
        <p>Two birds means two complete document sets. This is where a lot of pair listings quietly fall apart, because papering one bird is cheaper than papering two.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">Two Birds Means Two Complete Document Sets</h3>
        <p>Each grey leaves here with its own CITES Appendix I documentation, its own DNA sexing certificate, its own avian veterinary health certificate, and its own hatch certificate carrying its band number. Nothing is shared and nothing is summarised onto one page.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">DNA Sexing on Both Birds, Not Just One</h3>
        <p><a href="/dna-tested-african-grey-for-sale/">Our DNA-sexing process</a> runs on every bird we list, because a grey is monomorphic and nobody can sex one by eye. A pair sold with one certificate is a pair where somebody guessed. ↗</p>
        <figure class="sec-img-wrap">
          <img class="sec-img inf-img inf-tall" src={`${IMG}/two-birds-two-document-sets.webp`} width="768" height="1376" style={"aspect-ratio:768/1376"}
               alt="Two complete document stacks, one per grey, covering CITES, DNA sexing, vet health and hatch records"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async"  srcset={`${String(`${IMG}/two-birds-two-document-sets.webp`).replace(/(-\d{2,4})?(\.[a-zA-Z0-9]+)$/, '-600$2')} 600w, ${`${IMG}/two-birds-two-document-sets.webp`} 768w`} sizes="(max-width:640px) 92.1vw, 420px" />
          <figcaption class="img-note">Two birds, two files. Nothing is shared and nothing is summarised onto one page.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h4 class="cag-h4">Do You Need Separate CITES Papers for Each Grey?</h4>
        <p>Yes. The documentation attaches to the bird, not to the transaction, and a pair is two birds.</p>
      </section>

