      <!-- ═══ §16 HEALTH ═══ -->
      <section id="health">
        <h2 class="cag-h2">What Health Screening Do Both Birds Clear Before They Ship?</h2>
        <p>Every bird we list is PCR screened for PBFD and polyomavirus and examined by an avian veterinarian. With a pair that screening carries extra weight.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">PBFD and Polyomavirus PCR on Every Bird We List</h3>
        <p>Both diseases are screened by PCR rather than by observation, on both birds, before either is listed. <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Peer-reviewed literature on circovirus transmission in psittacines</a> is unambiguous that close contact is the main route, which is exactly what a pair is. ↗</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">Why a Pair Raises the Stakes on Disease Screening</h3>
        <p>Two birds in constant contact share everything. An unscreened pair is not two independent risks, it is one shared one — and it is why we will not sell a pair where only one bird has been tested.</p>
        <figure class="sec-img-wrap">
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={`${IMG}/pair-health-screening-pcr-panel.webp`} width="1376" height="768" style={"aspect-ratio:1376/768"}
               alt="The PCR screening panel and avian veterinary examination both birds clear before either one ships"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async"  srcset={`${String(`${IMG}/pair-health-screening-pcr-panel.webp`).replace(/(-\d{2,4})?(\.[a-zA-Z0-9]+)$/, '-480$2')} 480w, ${`${IMG}/pair-health-screening-pcr-panel.webp`} 1376w`} sizes="(max-width:1024px) 100vw, 59.4vw" />
          <figcaption class="img-note">Both birds, not a sample of one. Neither ships until both results are back.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h4 class="cag-h4">What Happens If One Bird of a Pair Tests Positive?</h4>
        <p>Neither ships. We do not split a pair to move the healthy half, and we do not hold the result back to save a sale. <a href="/african-greys-for-sale-with-health-guarantee/">The written health guarantee behind every bird</a> runs seventy-two hours from arrival, with a twenty-four-hour window on shipping. ↗</p>
      </section>

