      <!-- ═══ §17 LEGAL ═══ -->
      <section id="legal">
        <h2 class="cag-h2">Is It Legal to Own Two Captive-Bred African Greys in the United States?</h2>
        <p>Yes, with the right paperwork, and owning two changes nothing about the legal position beyond doubling the documents.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">CITES Appendix I and What It Means for Domestic Transfer</h3>
        <p><a href="https://cites.org/eng/app/appendices.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The CITES appendices listing</a> places <em>Psittacus erithacus</em> in Appendix I, which governs international trade. Captive-bred birds are legal to own and transfer domestically with proper documentation, and every bird we place is captive-bred in the USA. ↗</p>
        <figure class="sec-img-wrap">
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={`${IMG}/cites-appendix-one-two-birds-usa.webp`} width="1376" height="768" style={"aspect-ratio:1376/768"}
               alt="What CITES Appendix I status means for owning and transferring two captive-bred greys inside the USA"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async"  srcset={`${String(`${IMG}/cites-appendix-one-two-birds-usa.webp`).replace(/(-\d{2,4})?(\.[a-zA-Z0-9]+)$/, '-480$2')} 480w, ${`${IMG}/cites-appendix-one-two-birds-usa.webp`} 1376w`} sizes="(max-width:1024px) 100vw, 59.4vw" />
          <figcaption class="img-note">Appendix I governs international trade. Captive-bred birds transfer domestically with their papers.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h4 class="cag-h4">Does Owning Two Birds Change Your Legal Obligations?</h4>
        <p>Not materially. You keep two sets of papers instead of one. <a href="https://www.aphis.usda.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USDA APHIS animal-care licensing information</a> covers the breeder side of that arrangement rather than the owner side. ↗</p>
        <h5 class="cag-h5">Appendix I Since CoP17, Effective January 2017</h5>
        <p>The uplisting from Appendix II took effect in January 2017. Any seller still describing greys as Appendix II is working from stale information, and that is worth noticing.</p>
      </section>

