      <!-- ═══ §19 SETTLING IN ═══ -->
      <section id="settling">
        <h2 class="cag-h2">How Do You Settle Two New Greys Into Your Home?</h2>
        <p>The first month sets the pattern for the next forty years, and with two birds it is the month that decides whether you get a pair or a flock of two that tolerates you.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">The First Thirty Days, Cage by Cage</h3>
        <p>Week one is separate cages and, if you keep other birds, separate rooms. Week two brings the cages into the same room with no contact. Weeks three and four allow supervised time out together, always watched. Only after a month, and only once both birds are calm, would we leave them unsupervised.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">Quarantine If You Already Keep Birds</h3>
        <p>Thirty days minimum, in a separate airspace, before any new grey meets an existing bird. Both of ours arrive screened, but screening is not a substitute for quarantine.</p>
        <figure class="sec-img-wrap">
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={`${IMG}/introducing-two-african-greys-first-30-days.webp`} width="1376" height="768" style={"aspect-ratio:1376/768"}
               alt="A week-by-week timeline for settling two new African Greys into one home across the first month"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async"  srcset={`${String(`${IMG}/introducing-two-african-greys-first-30-days.webp`).replace(/(-\d{2,4})?(\.[a-zA-Z0-9]+)$/, '-480$2')} 480w, ${`${IMG}/introducing-two-african-greys-first-30-days.webp`} 1376w`} sizes="(max-width:1024px) 100vw, 59.4vw" />
          <figcaption class="img-note">Four weeks, cage by cage. Never start two new greys in one cage on day one.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h4 class="cag-h4">How Long Before You Let Them Interact Unsupervised?</h4>
        <p>A month, at the earliest, and longer if either bird is showing territorial behaviour at the cage bars.</p>
        <h5 class="cag-h5">Introduce Across a Gap Before You Ever Share a Cage</h5>
        <p>Every introduction we have seen go badly started with two birds put straight into one cage on day one.</p>
        <h6 class="cag-h6"><span class="h6k">Two-Bird Note:</span> The Thirty-Day Separation We Ask Every Pair Buyer to Keep</h6>
        <p class="note">It is the one thing we ask of pair buyers, and it costs nothing but patience. <a href="/african-grey-parrot-care-guide/">Our full care routine</a> covers the rest of that first month. ↗</p>
      </section>

